  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Bihar now known for development, not scams and crimes: PM targets Cong-RJD",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/bihar-known-for-development-not-scams-and-crimes-pm-targets-cong-rjd-126112100505_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Saturday made a stinging attack on the opposition RJD-Congress alliance in Bihar, asserting that the state, under the NDA's rule, was making news for development and investments \"in place of scams and crimes\".\nModi addressed a rally in Jafarpatti of Vaishali district, about 50 km from the state capital, where he dedicated to the nation projects worth more than Rs 34,000 crore, including a bridge over the Ganga. The bridge has been named 'Nitish Setu'.\nThe PM, who delivered a relatively short speech, said that he was short on time and had to visit the adjoining Uttar Pradesh.\nHe said the bridge was named after the JD(U) president, who gave up the post of chief minister in April to make way for a BJP-helmed government, \"as a mark of respect for his contributions to the state\".\n\"The state has come a long way since the NDA took over. Earlier, only scams and crimes were talked about. Now Bihar makes news for investment proposals and action taken against .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-21T10:43:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "PM Modi to launch development projects worth ₹34,470 cr in Bihar's Vaishali",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/pm-modi-to-launch-development-projects-worth-34-470-cr-in-bihar-s-vaishali-126112100166_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi will visit Bihar's Vaishali district on Saturday to launch projects worth nearly 34,470 crore, including a six-lane bridge over the Ganga river, and address a public meeting, officials said.\nThis would be the Prime Minister's first visit to the eastern state since May, when he had attended a function marking the expansion of the cabinet headed by Chief Minister Samrat Choudhary, the first BJP leader to lead a government in Bihar.\nElaborate security arrangements, including the suspension of vehicular movement on the national and state highways concerned for a stipulated period, have been made in Vaishali and Patna for the PM's visit, they said.\nThe 9.76-km-long six-lane bridge, which connects Bidupur block in Vaishali to Kachchi Dargah on the outskirts of Patna, has been named 'Nitish Setu', in deference to the former Bihar chief minister, on whose watch the project was conceived and came close to completion.\n\"The PM will visit 'Nitish Setu' in Vaishali.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-21T05:01:34"
    }
  ]
